<article class="env-lemma" id="042R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/042R">Lemma <span data-tag="042R">67.10.7</span>.</a> An immersion of algebraic spaces is a monomorphism. In particular, any immersion is separated. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $f : X \to Y$ be an immersion of algebraic spaces. For any morphism $Z \to Y$ with $Z$ representable the base change $Z \times _ Y X \to Z$ is an immersion of schemes, hence a monomorphism, see Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01L7" data-tag="01L7">26.23.8</a>. Hence $f$ is representable, and a monomorphism. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>